				769,
				123
			],
			"Message": "style(Output): Minify ESBuild configuration and plugin pipeline source modules\n\nRemove verbose comments, blank lines, and redundant formatting across the Output component's build pipeline. The ESBuild configuration modules, 50+ transform plugins, runtime polyfills, and CEL services are compressed to minimal readable form while preserving all functional logic.\n\nChanges span:\n- ESBuild entry configurations (Editor, VSCode, Output) and exclusion modules\n- Plugin pipeline: Copy, Transform, Polyfill namespaces with 50+ plugins\n- Runtime polyfills: ChildProcess, FileProtocol, FileSystem, IPCRenderer, NativeModule, Process, SharedProcessProxy, Telemetry\n- CEL services: ExposeAccessor, ExtensionsScanner, Null services, SearchService, SharedProcessService, DevLog, TauriMainProcessService with MistWebSocketTransport, Trace\n\nThis reduces source size by ~40% and improves build pipeline readability. No behavioral changes — all transforms, polyfills, and service contracts remain identical.",
			"SHA": "20812430b9708294d8e0a941dcb230d9bdbc91e6"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-11T02:30:47Z",
			"File": [
				"⡿⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				769,
				126
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Output): Restructure build pipeline, plugin system, and runtime polyfills for Tauri compatibility\n\nPromote all ESBuild configuration and plugin source modules from the nested\n`Configuration/Element/Output/Source/` tree to the `Configuration/` root,\ncreating a flat, reproducible layout where source-of-truth modules live\nalongside their compiled `.js`/`.js.map` artifacts. This eliminates the\nsplit-source problem that hindered source-level debugging and version-controlled\nevolution of the bundling logic.\n\nESBuild Configuration:\n- Add comprehensive exclusion modules (Bootstrap, Electron, Node, Network,\n  Telemetry, Test, Types, WebWorker, Workbench, Chromium IPC, NLS, Server,\n  Standalone, Potential, BuiltIn) that declaratively strip VS Code's Electron\n  workbench, Node platform, telemetry appenders, update service, extension\n  gallery, and test code from the bundle.\n- Define Editor and VSCode entry configurations with conditional Rest compiler\n  integration (`Compiler=Rest`), PostHog build telemetry (debug-only), and\n  target cleanup via `Clean=true`.\n- Add `outbase` to VSCode config so `vs/base/common/uri.js` lands at\n  `Target/Microsoft/VSCode/vs/base/common/uri.js` instead of the full\n  Dependency path.\n\nPlugin Pipeline (50+ transforms):\n- Copy plugins: VS output, VS root files (with inline NLS stubs), Tauri main\n  process service, Worker, Node modules (@xterm/*, vscode-textmate, etc.),\n  unpublished addon stubs, and dependency supplements.\n- Transform plugins: Name shim, Worker bootstrap shim, nested worker rewrite,\n  perf baseline worker rewrite, Node modules path rewrite, webview polyfills,\n  worker/workbench base URL rewrites, static block self-ref rewrite, function\n  declaration hoisting, Electron IPC/shared process/extension gallery/search/\n  telemetry/update/service replacements, output folder rejection catch,\n  webview iframe sandbox strip, workbench accessor expose, VS Code Git\n  instrumentation, unused service disable, configuration/storage overlays,\n  icons stylesheet URL rewrite, macOS titlebar offset CSS, part z-index CSS,\n  Tauri drag region, telemetry consent off, editor/terminal GPU layer CSS,\n  webview blob URL rewrite, webview debug logging, webview runtime diagnostics,\n  workbench interactivity/paint priming, worker bootstrap shim, CSS import\n  inlining/stripping, static-to-dynamic import, dangling source map strip.\n\nRuntime Polyfills (browser/Tauri environment):\n- ChildProcess: Full `child_process` API via Mountain IPC (spawn, exec, fork).\n- FileProtocol: `vscode-file:`, `vscode-userdata:`, `vscode-resource:`,\n  `vscode-remote:`, `file:` fetch interception backed by Mountain file ops.\n- FileSystem: Complete `fs`/`fs.promises` API via Mountain (`readFile`,\n  `writeFile`, `stat`, `readdir`, `mkdir`, `rm`, `copyFile`, `rename`, `exists`).\n- IPCRenderer: Electron `ipcRenderer` shim routing 40+ channels to Mountain\n  via gRPC (logger, policy, sign, userDataProfiles, localFileSystem, storage,\n  configuration, commands, search, terminal, extensions, nativeHost, git, etc.).\n- NativeModule: Electron module stubs (app, dialog, clipboard, shell, screen,\n  webFrame, BrowserWindow, nativeTheme) backed by Tauri APIs.\n- Process: Node `process` polyfill with Tauri-backed `execPath`, `pid`,\n  `platform`, `arch`, `versions`, `hrtime`, `cpuUsage`, `getProcessMemoryInfo`.\n- SharedProcessProxy: Service proxies for extension-host, search, debug,\n  storage, update with correlation-ID request/response over Mountain IPC.\n- Telemetry: No-op `__LAND_POLYFILL_TELEMETRY__` sink for polyfill error reporting.\n\nCEL Services (injected into workbench instantiation):\n- ExposeAccessor: Binds 50+ workbench services to `globalThis.__CEL_SERVICES__`\n  for downstream polyfill consumption; patches `activateByEvent` to short-circuit\n  `onView:*` events; captures webview MessagePorts for extension host bridging.\n- ExtensionsScanner: Mountain-backed `scanSystemExtensions`/`scanUserExtensions`\n  with retry scheduling and telemetry tracing.\n- NullExtensionGallery/NullTelemetry/NullUpdate: No-op stubs replacing marketplace,\n  telemetry, and auto-update services (extensions sideloaded from `~/.fiddee/`).\n- SearchService: Mountain-backed `RemoteSearchService` (file + text search via\n  `search:findFiles`/`search:findInFiles` gRPC) + `LocalFileSearchWorkerClient`.\n- SharedProcessService: Thin wrapper over `TauriMainProcessService` for shared\n  process emulation.\n- DevLog: Tag-filtered, deduplicated dev logging with `Trace` localStorage config.\n- TauriMainProcessService: 60+ channel router (`ChannelRouteMap`) mapping VS Code\n  IPC channels to Mountain gRPC prefixes; per-channel tier resolution (Mountain,\n  Node, WebSocket via Mist); comprehensive stub channels for unimplemented\n  services (sign, policy, keyboardLayout, update, webview, diagnostics, etc.);\n  Mist WebSocket transport with exponential backoff reconnect and binary\n  envelope protocol.\n- Trace: `performance.mark`/`measure` helpers with `$APP` path aliasing.\n\nShell Scripts:\n- Normalize `Source/Run.sh` and `Source/prepublishOnly.sh` case statement\n  indentation and branch formatting (no logic changes).\n\nThis ensures the repository tracks only source-of-truth configuration while\nenabling reproducible builds, source-level debugging of the build pipeline, and\nversion-controlled evolution of the Output component's bundling logic. The\nESBuild configuration supports Rest compiler integration (conditional via\n`Compiler=Rest`), PostHog build telemetry (debug-only), target cleanup via\n`Clean=true`, and declarative exclusion/transform pipelines that rewrite VS\nCode's Electron workbench for Tauri/WKWebView compatibility. Cocoon continues\nto consume fresh builds from `Configuration/` at runtime via the existing pipeline.",
			"SHA": "61cb3a9fcda1b193537c99906e4f0bf45a6cd9ac"
		},
